assistant: Subject: Parse epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as a number of epoch milliseconds (1792142857943) instead of an ISO string. `get_order` passed it through `Date.parse(String(...))`, which returns NaN for a plain number string, and the `|| 0` fallback turned that into the 1970-01-01 date. The fix changes only `src/tools/get_order.ts`: number values now go straight to `new Date()`, so this order returns 2026-10-16T09:27:37.943Z. String values are still parsed as ISO, so the v1 output is unchanged. I also removed the silent fallback to 1970. If `created_at` can't be read at all, the tool now returns an error instead of a made-up date. Your rules say not to return errors in place of data, so say if you'd rather handle that differently; it doesn't affect any order that has a readable date. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass.

